55,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A is simple, but the taster forms show it scares people off. Option B might be too rigid.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Option C is a treasurer's nightmare. I strongly oppose activity-based charging.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option B allows us to differentiate between the regulars and the occasional visitors.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option B sounds like it creates ""grades,"" which could make the quieter members feel even more uneasy.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A gives us the most predictable income for those fixed costs.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, wouldn't tiered membership just make the ""invisible"" members feel more judged?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, A is stable, but the bank statements show people struggle to pay it all at once.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, but B could lower the entry barrier for those who only come twice a year.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"I prefer A. It's a ""you belong"" fee. Once you pay, you just show up.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"I agree with Shunichi. We can't risk the budget on ""pay-as-you-go"" habits.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we choose A, we should perhaps allow monthly installments to help those who struggle.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,That would be a reasonable compromise to keep the administration simple but accessible.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I still feel B is the only way to address the unfairness of the workload.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Fairness is less important than the club's survival and spirit, Jonathan.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I'm voting for A. It's the only way to ensure the account doesn't run dry.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I'll go with A as well. It's the cleanest for newcomers if we handle the payment flexibility.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,A is the most rational choice for the treasurer's sanity.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I'll stick with B, but I see the majority is leaning elsewhere.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,A it is.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Takumi,,Let's vote.,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
